<h1>Arrange Labels</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Labels &gt; Arrange</b></span> in Inspection mode or from the <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>label context menu</b></span> in <span class="Mode" style="text-decoration:underline;"><u>Edit label</u></span> mode.</p>
<p class="Description" style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-US">Description:</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span lang="EN-US">This command arranges automatically all labels in the current page at the borders of the viewport.</span></p>
<p class="USE" style="margin-left:48px; text-indent:-24px;"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: For arranging manually placed labels in a page. If some actions as translate, rotate or zoom are performed on a compared object in Inspection mode, the object itself will be moved or zoomed, but the connected labels will remain at their positions. The connections between the labels and their correspondent points will look mixed-up. The</span> <span class="Command">Arrange Labels</span> <span lang="EN-US">command is very useful in similar cases.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-US">: There will be no visible result if the</span> <span class="Command">Auto Arrange Labels</span> <span lang="EN-US">option is active.</span></p>

